# .secretsignore - paths mask_secrets.py does not scan.
#
# Syntax is gitignore-like: one glob per line, "#" starts a comment,
# "!" negates a previous match.  The file is resolved from the git root and
# from every scanned directory (see tools/secrets/README.md).

# The test fixtures must contain realistic credential *formats* to prove that
# the detection rules work.  Every value there is invalid ("EXAMPLE" filler),
# so nothing sensitive lives in that file.  Keep it that way: never put a real
# credential in a fixture.
tools/secrets/tests/fixtures.py

# Local, untracked material that must never be pushed anyway.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!sample.env
secrets/
